Hybrid Simulation Gains Momentum
While pure Discrete Event Simulation remains a foundational methodology for manufacturing, logistics, and healthcare applications, hybrid simulation is gaining attention.
Hybrid approaches can combine DES with agent-based modeling or system dynamics, enabling organizations to analyze more complex systems where individual entity behavior, discrete events, and long-term system-level changes interact.
This capability is particularly valuable for applications such as supply chain resilience, autonomous vehicle logistics, public safety, strategic planning, and complex industrial ecosystems.
